## Brief (required — the ONLY required field)

_One paragraph. What is the product? Who is it for? Why does it exist?_

_Write in plain language. You can be vague about tech ("like Spotify but
for audiobooks") or specific ("a React PWA for restaurant owners"). The
library will fill in the rest._

**A good brief always answers three things: WHO it's for, WHAT they
can do with it, and WHY it matters.** If you cover those three, the
rest is optional.

> **Worked example** — a complete brief:
>
> > A room-booking app for a 10-person yoga studio in Portland.
> > Customers book and pay for classes from their phones; the owner
> > manages the weekly schedule and sees who paid, from a simple
> > dashboard.
>
> **What the library infers from it:**
> - _Who / what / why:_ customers (book + pay for classes), the studio
>   owner (manage schedule, track payments) — the "why" is a studio
>   too small for off-the-shelf booking software.
> - _Platforms:_ "from their phones" → iPhone + Android apps; "simple
>   dashboard" → website. (All three — the default holds.)
> - _Users / roles:_ Customer, Studio Owner (an admin role is implied).
> - _Baseline:_ logins, payments (Stripe), an admin panel, notifications
>   for booking confirmations.
> - _Non-goals:_ no class-content streaming, no multi-studio support,
>   no waitlist marketplace — none of that was asked for.
>
> **Warning:** the vaguer your brief, the more the library assumes —
> more platforms, more baseline features, more tasks. A one-liner like
> "a fitness app" gets the maximum defaults: the longest, most
> expensive run. Two specific sentences beat a vague paragraph.

### Alternative: answer 3 questions instead

_If the blank box above feels intimidating, delete it and answer these
three questions instead. (The Quick Start agent asks one question and
infers the rest — these three are for when you're filling this file in
yourself.)_

1. **What should people be able to DO with this?** (the 2–3 most
   important actions — e.g. "book a class, pay for it, cancel it")
2. **Who is it for, specifically?** ("yoga studio owners with under 20
   staff" — not "users")
3. **What does success look like on day one?** (the one outcome that
   matters most — e.g. "a customer can book and pay without calling
   the studio")

