## Defaults the library will assume if you leave the rest blank

**Leave everything below blank and you get: a website + iPhone app +
Android app, with logins, an admin panel, and app-store packaging.**
That's the full production default — great if you might grow, overkill
for a weekend MVP. If you want less, say so under **Restrict** below
(there are copy-paste recipes).

Skip ahead and leave the sections below empty if any of these defaults
are fine. Only edit them if you want to **restrict** the scope or
**override** a default.

<details>
<summary>Exact technical defaults (click to expand)</summary>

- **Platforms**: web (responsive, PWA-capable) + Android + iOS. All three.
- **Web stack**: React 18 + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind. Next.js if the
  brief implies server-rendered pages.
- **Mobile stack**: native Kotlin/Jetpack Compose on Android, native
  Swift/SwiftUI on iOS. React Native only if the brief asks for
  "cross-platform" or similar.
- **Backend stack**: Node.js + Fastify + PostgreSQL + Redis. Python/
  Django or Go/Gin only if the brief mentions domain constraints that
  favour them (ML, high-throughput, etc.).
- **Hosting**: prefers free-tier / freemium managed services
  (Vercel / Netlify / Railway / Supabase / Neon / Fly.io) for hobby and
  MVP scale; AWS ECS + RDS for anything that hints at production scale.
- **Auth**: email + password + OAuth (Google, Apple) with JWT +
  refresh tokens. Biometric on mobile (Face ID / Touch ID /
  Fingerprint).
- **Data storage**: PostgreSQL for relational; object storage (S3 /
  R2 / Supabase Storage) for blobs; Redis for cache + queues.
- **Production readiness baseline** (generated when relevant):
  onboarding & consent, account identity when accounts are in scope,
  admin portal + RBAC when roles/backends are in scope, observability
  (structured logs + metrics +
  error tracking), localization (i18n + RTL), theming (dark + light
  mode, decoupled tokens for whitelabeling), accessibility (WCAG 2.1
  AA), automated tests (unit + integration + UI + e2e), CI/CD
  pipelines, infra-as-code, app store release assets for mobile,
  user onboarding, settings + debug menu, privacy + PII controls +
  consent flows.

</details>

If you want any of those turned **off**, list them under **Restrict**
below.

