## Restrict (optional — turn OFF parts of the production-readiness baseline)

_This is the highest-leverage section in this file: every line here
shrinks the plan. The library generates the full production-readiness
baseline by default — web + iPhone + Android, logins, admin panel,
app-store packaging, the works. List here any baseline topics you DO
NOT want generated._

**Copy-paste recipes** (pick one, paste it below, delete the `…` line):

_Web-only MVP — the single biggest time-saver (roughly two-thirds
fewer tasks for a typical brief):_
```
Web only — no iOS app, no Android app, no app-store release assets.
```

_No mobile apps in v1 — keep the full web build, defer mobile:_
```
No mobile apps in v1 — web + backend + admin panel only. Keep the
API mobile-ready so apps can be added later.
```

_No app-store release — build the apps, skip the store submission work:_
```
Build the iOS and Android apps, but skip app-store release assets
(screenshots, store listings, release packaging).
```

_Or write your own, e.g.:_
- No admin panel — single owner, no staff roles.
- No Infrastructure as Code — deploy to a managed host instead.

